1
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:45,962
‪SPOOKY IN LOVE

2
00:00:55,972 --> 00:00:57,599
‪Are you sure about this?

3
00:00:59,809 --> 00:01:01,186
‪Yes, I'm sure.

4
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:05,648
‪After all, I'm the only person
‪you can comfortably share

5
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:08,193
‪your everyday life with.

6
00:01:09,027 --> 00:01:12,072
‪I'm sorry for making you lie.

7
00:01:12,155 --> 00:01:13,531
‪No, don't be sorry.

8
00:01:14,532 --> 00:01:16,201
‪I'm actually grateful

9
00:01:16,284 --> 00:01:18,411
‪that you trusted me enough
‪to ask for help.

10
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,211
‪So why does the chairwoman

11
00:01:26,294 --> 00:01:28,505
‪want you to marry Kang Min-hwan?

12
00:01:30,298 --> 00:01:31,174
‪It beats me.

13
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:35,386
‪Whatever the reason, let's make this work.

14
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:37,055
‪Sure.

15
00:01:37,138 --> 00:01:38,181
‪Good luck to us.

16
00:01:44,270 --> 00:01:46,064
‪EPISODE 7

17
00:01:46,147 --> 00:01:47,732
‪Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk and I…

18
00:01:49,317 --> 00:01:50,568
‪are getting engaged.

19
00:02:07,544 --> 00:02:08,711
‪Secretaries, leave us.

20
00:02:10,839 --> 00:02:15,260
‪Director Gong, could you excuse us
‪for this family matter?

21
00:02:30,608 --> 00:02:31,442
‪Yeo-ri.

22
00:02:32,443 --> 00:02:34,404
‪What are you doing with our guests here?

23
00:02:35,488 --> 00:02:36,781
‪In front of Min-hwan, of all people.

24
00:02:37,448 --> 00:02:40,034
‪I was going to tell you soon. I'm sorry.

25
00:02:40,785 --> 00:02:44,289
‪You know I keep to myself
‪until I'm absolutely certain.

26
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:48,877
‪Are you saying
‪you're certain about this then?

27
00:02:49,752 --> 00:02:50,837
‪Yes.

28
00:02:53,923 --> 00:02:55,216
‪It doesn't seem like it.

29
00:02:55,717 --> 00:02:58,928
‪I get the feeling
‪that this is an improvised act.

30
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:00,972
‪What do you mean?

31
00:03:01,055 --> 00:03:01,973
‪Think about it.

32
00:03:02,056 --> 00:03:05,476
‪The whole country knows
‪about your failed dating history,

33
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:08,271
‪yet you show up
‪not just with a boyfriend but a fiancé.

34
00:03:08,354 --> 00:03:09,230
‪Am I wrong?

35
00:03:10,064 --> 00:03:12,692
‪Min-hwan, I'm so sorry.

36
00:03:13,276 --> 00:03:15,445
‪-How about we do this another--
‪-No.

37
00:03:16,863 --> 00:03:18,781
‪How about we just eat?

38
00:03:18,865 --> 00:03:20,825
‪I'd like to hear more over the meal.

39
00:03:21,659 --> 00:03:22,493
‪I'm curious to hear

40
00:03:23,328 --> 00:03:27,540
‪when the two of them
‪got close enough to get engaged.

41
00:03:27,624 --> 00:03:29,500
‪To be honest, when we last met,

42
00:03:30,501 --> 00:03:32,503
‪I didn't get that impression at all.

43
00:03:32,587 --> 00:03:34,547
‪That's what dating in secret is like.

44
00:03:35,256 --> 00:03:37,425
‪How long have you been together?

45
00:03:37,508 --> 00:03:38,718
‪-A year.
‪-Six months.

46
00:03:39,969 --> 00:03:41,054
‪-A year.
‪-Six months.

47
00:03:43,765 --> 00:03:46,476
‪Gosh, I got a bit confused.

48
00:03:46,559 --> 00:03:48,144
‪We met a year ago,

49
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:50,855
‪but we only started dating six months ago.

50
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:54,609
‪Goodness. I wonder how you first met.

51
00:03:54,692 --> 00:03:57,487
‪-You don't just run into Yeo-ri by chance.
‪-Exactly.

52
00:03:58,154 --> 00:03:59,906
‪We rarely see her ourselves.

53
00:03:59,989 --> 00:04:03,034
‪Where exactly did you two first meet?

54
00:04:03,117 --> 00:04:04,494
‪-On a mountain.
‪-On a mountain.

55
00:04:04,577 --> 00:04:05,578
‪On a mountain?

56
00:04:06,454 --> 00:04:08,081
‪That's funny. Doing what?

57
00:04:08,164 --> 00:04:09,999
‪We were both hiking, of course.

58
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:12,377
‪Yeo-ri doesn't hike outdoors.

59
00:04:13,127 --> 00:04:16,381
‪-She only does indoor climbing.
‪-No, I do go outdoors.

60
00:04:16,464 --> 00:04:18,841
‪I hike mountains,

61
00:04:18,925 --> 00:04:21,386
‪and I jog along the Han River too.

62
00:04:21,469 --> 00:04:25,306
‪-You go all the way to the river to jog?
‪-Exactly. I live far from the river,

63
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:29,644
‪so I jog along the Han River,
‪and I eat <i>‪ramyeon</i>‪ too.

64
00:04:29,727 --> 00:04:32,855
‪You ate<i>‪ ramyeon</i>‪ by the Han River?

65
00:04:33,898 --> 00:04:35,275
‪It's delicious.

66
00:04:35,358 --> 00:04:37,235
‪-No way.
‪-That's impossible.

67
00:04:37,318 --> 00:04:39,153
‪I know you well, Yeo-ri.

68
00:04:40,613 --> 00:04:41,531
‪How is that even possible?

69
00:04:45,326 --> 00:04:46,744
‪-Because we're in love.
‪-Because we're in love.

70
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:53,376
‪You two. Can I have a word?

71
00:05:10,143 --> 00:05:12,603
‪There's no need to be nervous.
‪It'll be fine.

72
00:05:12,687 --> 00:05:14,856
‪I know. I'm not nervous.

73
00:05:24,282 --> 00:05:25,491
‪-Have a seat.
‪-Yes, ma'am.

74
00:05:31,331 --> 00:05:33,708
‪You could've at least given me a heads-up.

75
00:05:34,292 --> 00:05:36,461
‪But this is how you do things,

76
00:05:36,544 --> 00:05:38,463
‪bulldozing right ahead without warning.

77
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:42,800
‪You have a point,
‪but why didn't you tell me beforehand?

78
00:05:42,884 --> 00:05:44,886
‪You didn't have to
‪put Min-hwan through that.

79
00:05:45,928 --> 00:05:47,930
‪I know what you're worried about, Grandma.

80
00:05:48,514 --> 00:05:50,349
‪But Min-hwan and I

81
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:53,186
‪don't have any feelings for each other.

82
00:05:53,811 --> 00:05:57,648
‪If you're worried about our business,
‪that's even more reason not to do it.

83
00:05:58,399 --> 00:06:02,195
‪So your relationship with Mr. Ma
‪isn't purely business?

84
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:03,905
‪What?

85
00:06:03,988 --> 00:06:05,615
‪Are you sure
‪you have feelings for each other?

86
00:06:07,909 --> 00:06:09,077
‪Yes, I'm sure.

87
00:06:09,827 --> 00:06:10,953
‪What about you, Mr. Ma?

88
00:06:11,037 --> 00:06:11,996
‪Pardon?

89
00:06:13,498 --> 00:06:15,541
‪We feel the same about each other.

90
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:17,877
‪Let him speak for himself.

91
00:06:18,377 --> 00:06:19,879
‪So how do you feel?

92
00:06:22,006 --> 00:06:23,716
‪Well, of course…

93
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:27,804
‪I care for Yeo-ri deeply.

94
00:06:34,894 --> 00:06:36,437
‪Enough to want to get engaged.

95
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:55,414
‪DIRECTOR OF YEEON

96
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:58,167
‪Excuse me for a moment.

97
00:06:58,251 --> 00:06:59,961
‪-I need to take this.
‪-Hurry back.

98
00:07:06,259 --> 00:07:07,301
‪Hello, Director.

99
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:10,680
‪What did they find?

100
00:07:14,016 --> 00:07:15,685
‪I'll be right there. Bye.

101
00:07:21,274 --> 00:07:22,108
‪Min-hwan.

102
00:07:24,402 --> 00:07:26,195
‪I'm sorry about what happened earlier.

103
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:28,114
‪My grandma went too far.

104
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:32,702
‪It wouldn't have been so uncomfortable
‪if she'd told me you'd be here.

105
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:35,663
‪It wasn't your grandmother's fault.

106
00:07:36,456 --> 00:07:37,540
‪I wanted to join the dinner.

107
00:07:40,084 --> 00:07:40,960
‪Yeo-ri.

108
00:07:43,087 --> 00:07:44,130
‪I can guess why

109
00:07:44,797 --> 00:07:46,090
‪you went this far today.

110
00:07:50,511 --> 00:07:51,929
‪What do you mean?

111
00:08:06,652 --> 00:08:07,487
‪You can sit comfortably.

112
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:09,322
‪I'm comfortable.

113
00:08:14,076 --> 00:08:15,244
‪Have some tea.

114
00:08:16,662 --> 00:08:17,455
‪Thank you.

115
00:08:28,674 --> 00:08:29,842
‪Are you all right?

116
00:08:29,926 --> 00:08:31,344
‪Yes. It's refreshing.

117
00:08:33,930 --> 00:08:37,016
‪So what kind of prosecutor are you?

118
00:08:37,099 --> 00:08:40,645
‪I'm just an ordinary prosecutor,
‪like most others.

119
00:08:41,687 --> 00:08:42,730
‪I see.

120
00:08:43,981 --> 00:08:45,566
‪Do your parents

121
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:48,152
‪run a family business you might inherit?

122
00:08:48,861 --> 00:08:51,989
‪My parents passed away when I was young,
‪so my grandmother raised me.

123
00:08:52,490 --> 00:08:54,659
‪Do you still live with her?

124
00:08:54,742 --> 00:08:59,455
‪She retired to the countryside,
‪where she grows cabbages and beans.

125
00:09:02,208 --> 00:09:03,751
‪If you're done chatting,

126
00:09:03,834 --> 00:09:07,922
‪we should get going
‪to wrap up some work we have left.

127
00:09:08,005 --> 00:09:08,839
‪At this hour?

128
00:09:09,924 --> 00:09:10,841
‪We have a…

129
00:09:12,426 --> 00:09:13,427
‪date to finish.

130
00:09:27,024 --> 00:09:30,152
‪I was shocked earlier when Ms. Cheon
‪pulled that engagement ambush.

131
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:33,531
‪That wasn't an ambush.
‪She just brought it up to her family.

132
00:09:33,614 --> 00:09:37,201
‪-My hunch tells me it was staged--
‪-Oh, right.

133
00:09:37,285 --> 00:09:40,162
‪It's only been two months
‪since he came to return the shirt.

134
00:09:40,246 --> 00:09:41,372
‪-Two months?
‪-Yes.

135
00:09:41,455 --> 00:09:42,290
‪Then…

136
00:09:45,543 --> 00:09:47,670
‪Your grandmother
‪is incredibly charismatic.

137
00:09:48,337 --> 00:09:49,755
‪She's determined to push ahead,

138
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:52,258
‪-so we should prepare carefully.
‪-Right.

139
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:53,926
‪What?

140
00:09:55,136 --> 00:09:57,179
‪Right, what did Director Lee say?

141
00:09:57,847 --> 00:09:58,973
‪They found the coffin.

142
00:09:59,890 --> 00:10:00,975
‪So it really was there.

143
00:10:01,809 --> 00:10:03,102
‪I'll go ahead and report it.

144
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:19,702
‪It's a divorce case
‪a close friend of mine is working on.

145
00:10:20,953 --> 00:10:21,996
‪A divorce case?

146
00:10:22,747 --> 00:10:25,708
‪I'm sorry, but I don't handle divorces.

147
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:27,793
‪The total assets in dispute
‪are worth seven trillion won.

148
00:10:27,877 --> 00:10:29,170
‪The husband is the guilty party

149
00:10:29,253 --> 00:10:31,047
‪and the wife is a founding member
‪of the company.

150
00:10:32,006 --> 00:10:34,300
‪-If you win the case, you'd get…
‪-Hold on.

151
00:10:35,426 --> 00:10:38,804
‪If the assets in dispute
‪are valued at seven trillion won,

152
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:41,932
‪is this the B&CA Holdings
‪chairman's divorce lawsuit?

153
00:10:42,475 --> 00:10:44,560
‪The so-called divorce of the century?

154
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:47,355
‪You recently hired
‪the former Family Court chief.

155
00:10:47,438 --> 00:10:49,190
‪His reputation and your law firm's name

156
00:10:49,273 --> 00:10:50,566
‪should be enough to win the case.

157
00:10:51,692 --> 00:10:52,693
‪That's my friend's personal number.

158
00:10:55,029 --> 00:10:56,906
‪Well, of course we can take it on.

159
00:10:56,989 --> 00:10:59,075
‪-Cha & Yul is more than capable--
‪-In return,

160
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:02,495
‪the real reason
‪you broke up with Ms. Cheon…

161
00:11:03,079 --> 00:11:04,830
‪is to be kept to yourself.

162
00:11:14,006 --> 00:11:16,384
‪Friends don't have to shake hands.

163
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:19,595
‪I got them on my business trip to Europe.

164
00:11:20,429 --> 00:11:21,514
‪I thought they'd suit you.

165
00:11:28,396 --> 00:11:30,439
‪Why did you stop Cha Gi-u
‪from coming to dinner?

166
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:34,443
‪I called to ask what happened,
‪and he told me to ask you.

167
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:39,031
‪Yeah, but maybe
‪I shouldn't have stopped him.

168
00:11:39,615 --> 00:11:42,743
‪If I insisted on marrying Yeo-ri

169
00:11:42,827 --> 00:11:44,745
‪despite the bomb
‪you were going to drop today,

170
00:11:45,413 --> 00:11:47,498
‪the chairwoman would've been deeply moved.

171
00:11:48,249 --> 00:11:49,792
‪I shouldn't have gotten in the way.

172
00:11:49,875 --> 00:11:51,544
‪Then call Cha Gi-u right now.

173
00:11:52,211 --> 00:11:53,587
‪Can't we go and talk
‪to my grandma together?

174
00:11:56,173 --> 00:11:59,260
‪Why do you keep covering for Yeo-ri,
‪even after she rejected you?

175
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:02,054
‪There can be only one reason.

176
00:12:03,139 --> 00:12:05,349
‪You still haven't given up on her?

177
00:12:06,434 --> 00:12:07,852
‪Even when she's announced her engagement?

178
00:12:09,019 --> 00:12:10,438
‪There's no way Yeo-ri can get engaged,

179
00:12:11,689 --> 00:12:13,274
‪whether it's to Ma Gang-uk or anyone else.

180
00:12:32,001 --> 00:12:33,711
‪-Are you from the Korea Heritage Service?
‪-Yes.

181
00:12:34,462 --> 00:12:35,463
‪-Shall we?
‪-Sure.

182
00:12:38,174 --> 00:12:39,300
‪Go slowly.

183
00:12:42,845 --> 00:12:43,929
‪One of you come up now.

184
00:12:44,597 --> 00:12:45,598
‪-You sure?
‪-Yes.

185
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:46,807
‪-It's out.
‪-Wait!

186
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:48,934
‪-Wait.
‪-Hold it.

187
00:12:49,894 --> 00:12:51,562
‪You're here, Ms. Cheon.

188
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:54,231
‪Hello.

189
00:12:54,315 --> 00:12:56,484
‪We received a report
‪that you found buried heritage.

190
00:12:56,567 --> 00:12:57,401
‪Yes.

191
00:12:57,485 --> 00:13:02,031
‪Shouldn't the Korea Heritage Service
‪check what's inside the coffin first?

192
00:13:02,114 --> 00:13:04,617
‪That's why I had someone from the museum…

193
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:05,576
‪She's right.

194
00:13:05,659 --> 00:13:07,119
‪We must check the item first

195
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:09,163
‪before the site is cleared
‪for further excavation.

196
00:13:09,788 --> 00:13:11,665
‪If it's deemed buried heritage,

197
00:13:11,749 --> 00:13:14,084
‪as you know, all construction must halt.

198
00:13:15,544 --> 00:13:18,088
‪If it's deemed buried heritage?

199
00:13:18,881 --> 00:13:20,299
‪Yes, of course. Please go ahead.

200
00:13:34,647 --> 00:13:37,233
‪You can never be with that fool,

201
00:13:38,067 --> 00:13:39,652
‪in life or in death.

202
00:13:40,194 --> 00:13:42,363
‪I will keep your soul here with me.

203
00:13:43,364 --> 00:13:44,490
‪Do you understand?

204
00:15:30,387 --> 00:15:33,432
<i>‪May you two go wherever you wish</i>

205
00:15:34,058 --> 00:15:35,225
<i>‪and rest in peace.</i>

206
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:03,504
‪Did they leave together in peace?

207
00:16:06,048 --> 00:16:06,882
‪Yes.

208
00:16:08,133 --> 00:16:10,469
‪They left in peace, together.

209
00:16:13,389 --> 00:16:14,431
‪We've confirmed it's buried heritage.

210
00:16:15,265 --> 00:16:18,102
‪As of now, all construction is suspended.

211
00:16:22,564 --> 00:16:24,233
‪Oh, my goodness.

212
00:16:24,316 --> 00:16:29,238
‪I guess spirits really do exist
‪and remain in our realm.

213
00:16:29,321 --> 00:16:33,117
‪Just when we uncovered
‪Prince Gangpyeong's romantic poem,

214
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:35,452
‪the camellias suddenly bloomed
‪out of season.

215
00:16:35,953 --> 00:16:36,954
‪On top of that,

216
00:16:37,037 --> 00:16:41,041
‪we discovered Hwagyeongdang's mummy,
‪perfectly preserved after 300 years.

217
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:44,503
‪This isn't just some astonishing story.

218
00:16:44,586 --> 00:16:46,130
‪It's a miracle.

219
00:16:46,213 --> 00:16:47,423
‪Don't you agree?

220
00:16:48,048 --> 00:16:49,717
‪I don't think it's a miracle.

221
00:16:50,968 --> 00:16:51,802
‪It's the truth.

222
00:16:51,885 --> 00:16:53,637
‪The truth? About what?

223
00:16:54,221 --> 00:16:56,849
‪That even after 300 years,
‪what must be revealed will come to light.

224
00:16:56,932 --> 00:16:59,893
‪Yes, that's exactly it. My goodness.

225
00:17:00,936 --> 00:17:02,604
‪What will you do with Hwagyeongdang?

226
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:04,690
‪Well, I'm sure

227
00:17:04,773 --> 00:17:07,609
‪the Korea Heritage Service
‪will issue a notice.

228
00:17:07,693 --> 00:17:09,570
‪I'll discuss the details with them.

229
00:17:09,653 --> 00:17:12,239
‪Hwagyeongdang isn't exactly unclaimed

230
00:17:12,322 --> 00:17:13,824
‪since she's a member of my family.

231
00:17:13,907 --> 00:17:16,326
‪Once the legal formalities
‪are taken care of,

232
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:19,997
‪I'll consider burying her
‪next to Prince Gangpyeong.

233
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:21,874
‪I really don't think you should do that.

234
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:25,210
‪Why not?

235
00:17:25,294 --> 00:17:27,796
‪Because I don't think
‪she's a member of your family.

236
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:31,842
‪What on earth do you mean?

237
00:17:32,426 --> 00:17:35,054
‪The other half
‪of the love letter was found

238
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:37,139
‪in the home of Dowon's descendants.

239
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:39,558
‪As you can see,

240
00:17:39,641 --> 00:17:41,935
‪it has Hwagyeongdang's signature
‪and Dowon's seal.

241
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:44,855
‪My gosh.

242
00:17:45,731 --> 00:17:47,316
‪Goodness, how can this be?

243
00:17:49,359 --> 00:17:52,404
‪Hwagyeongdang's love letter
‪wasn't meant for Prince Gangpyeong.

244
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:54,448
‪It was meant for the painter Dowon.

245
00:17:55,574 --> 00:17:56,658
‪Oh, dear.

246
00:17:56,742 --> 00:17:58,619
‪I can't believe this.

247
00:17:59,203 --> 00:18:00,746
‪Does this mean

248
00:18:00,829 --> 00:18:04,166
‪Hwagyeongdang had an affair with Dowon?

249
00:18:04,875 --> 00:18:05,918
‪No.

250
00:18:06,001 --> 00:18:08,837
‪It was Prince Gangpyeong who came between
‪Hwagyeongdang and Dowon.

251
00:18:09,922 --> 00:18:13,884
‪To be precise, he used his power
‪and violence to force them apart.

252
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:17,179
‪Goodness.

253
00:18:18,722 --> 00:18:20,974
‪I don't believe this, Ms. Cheon.

254
00:18:21,058 --> 00:18:22,184
‪Did you see it yourself?

255
00:18:23,727 --> 00:18:25,687
‪What grounds do you have to say that?

256
00:18:25,771 --> 00:18:27,231
‪All you have is a piece of paper.

257
00:18:27,314 --> 00:18:28,899
‪You yourself took a single love letter,

258
00:18:28,982 --> 00:18:32,694
‪likened Prince Gangpyeong's
‪love story to <i>‪Ghost</i>‪,

259
00:18:33,362 --> 00:18:36,156
‪and turned him into
‪the greatest romantic of Joseon.

260
00:18:37,282 --> 00:18:40,494
‪If you want to bury Hwagyeongdang
‪with Prince Gangpyeong

261
00:18:40,577 --> 00:18:43,705
‪or use her for some marketing spiel
‪of your museum…

262
00:18:45,666 --> 00:18:46,667
‪go ahead.

263
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:49,837
‪Then I'll release the love letter
‪to the public.

264
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:52,005
‪Okay, fine.

265
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:53,340
‪All right.

266
00:18:54,091 --> 00:18:56,510
‪What exactly is it that you want?

267
00:18:56,593 --> 00:18:59,555
‪There's a law under the Act
‪on the Protection and Investigation

268
00:18:59,638 --> 00:19:01,140
‪of Buried Cultural Heritage

269
00:19:01,223 --> 00:19:04,184
‪that states if there is no next of kin
‪or if such kin can't be identified,

270
00:19:04,268 --> 00:19:06,770
‪the remains may be
‪researched or preserved.

271
00:19:07,354 --> 00:19:08,814
‪Simply put,

272
00:19:08,897 --> 00:19:11,483
‪you just have to sign away all claims
‪on Hwagyeongdang's mummy.

273
00:19:12,234 --> 00:19:15,445
‪You must have a lot of free time
‪for a prosecutor.

274
00:19:15,529 --> 00:19:16,655
‪I closed all my other cases today.

275
00:19:17,698 --> 00:19:19,324
‪Gosh, I really…

276
00:19:20,117 --> 00:19:21,743
‪I really don't understand.

277
00:19:22,327 --> 00:19:24,413
‪This doesn't concern you at all.

278
00:19:24,496 --> 00:19:27,040
‪She's just some woman
‪who died 300 years ago.

279
00:19:27,124 --> 00:19:28,584
‪Why are you going this far?

280
00:19:30,419 --> 00:19:32,087
‪Because it does concern me.

281
00:19:34,173 --> 00:19:36,425
‪Whether it was 300 years ago or today,

282
00:19:36,967 --> 00:19:38,594
‪every life deserves to be respected,

283
00:19:40,053 --> 00:19:43,182
‪because anyone can die a wrongful death.

284
00:19:47,352 --> 00:19:50,355
‪Think about it and give me a call.

285
00:20:07,831 --> 00:20:09,875
‪At first, I wondered

286
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:15,631
‪why you were so fixated
‪on a case that wasn't even current

287
00:20:16,381 --> 00:20:19,384
‪and so determined
‪to find a 300-year-old body.

288
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:24,348
‪Because to me,
‪it wasn't a 300-year-old case.

289
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:28,268
‪It was the case of someone
‪standing right in front of me.

290
00:20:31,063 --> 00:20:32,022
‪Exactly.

291
00:20:34,024 --> 00:20:36,193
‪To people like me,
‪only what we see is reality.

292
00:20:36,985 --> 00:20:38,028
‪Your reality

293
00:20:38,862 --> 00:20:41,365
‪includes a world the rest can't see.

294
00:20:42,407 --> 00:20:44,326
‪You even take their hand in that world.

295
00:20:45,661 --> 00:20:46,954
‪In this reality,

296
00:20:48,538 --> 00:20:50,499
‪you held my hand.

297
00:20:56,129 --> 00:20:57,089
‪Yeo-ri.

298
00:20:57,756 --> 00:21:00,592
‪How about we look into
‪what happened to you?

299
00:21:02,970 --> 00:21:05,138
‪You resolved a wrongful death
‪from 300 years ago.

300
00:21:05,222 --> 00:21:09,142
‪Don't you think we could solve
‪a 12-year-old case if we really tried?

301
00:21:22,614 --> 00:21:25,617
‪He seems ordinary, yet he stands out.

302
00:21:25,701 --> 00:21:26,618
‪PERSONAL INFORMATION: MA GANG-UK

303
00:21:26,702 --> 00:21:29,496
‪He's been on the elite path too.

304
00:21:29,579 --> 00:21:30,414
‪HEART TRANSPLANT, DAEHAN JUNGANG HOSPITAL

305
00:21:30,497 --> 00:21:32,416
‪What's this? He had heart surgery?

306
00:21:32,499 --> 00:21:33,417
‪Yes.

307
00:21:34,084 --> 00:21:35,544
‪That bothers me a bit.

308
00:21:36,586 --> 00:21:39,131
‪-How is he now?
‪-He doesn't seem to have health issues.

309
00:21:39,756 --> 00:21:41,508
‪Should I look into it further?

310
00:21:42,050 --> 00:21:42,884
‪Yes, in detail.

311
00:21:45,804 --> 00:21:46,805
‪By the way,

312
00:21:46,888 --> 00:21:49,891
‪what did you think about the two of them?

313
00:21:51,476 --> 00:21:52,352
‪Well…

314
00:22:00,736 --> 00:22:01,653
‪Why?

315
00:22:01,737 --> 00:22:03,405
‪What about it doesn't make sense?

316
00:22:03,989 --> 00:22:06,116
‪First, it makes no sense

317
00:22:06,199 --> 00:22:09,202
‪that you dated for six months
‪without us knowing.

318
00:22:09,995 --> 00:22:13,665
‪And I remember the look on your face
‪that day very clearly.

319
00:22:14,249 --> 00:22:15,500
‪What do you remember so clearly?

320
00:22:16,418 --> 00:22:19,546
‪CEO of the most luxurious hotel
‪in the country, Cheon Yeo-ri.

321
00:22:20,380 --> 00:22:22,049
<i>‪The look on your face that day</i>

322
00:22:22,632 --> 00:22:25,510
‪was of a man who had no clue
‪who Cheon Yeo-ri was.

323
00:22:26,303 --> 00:22:28,764
‪Hey, what do you mean I had no clue?

324
00:22:28,847 --> 00:22:31,600
‪I had to keep my work separate
‪from my personal life.

325
00:22:31,683 --> 00:22:32,809
‪Shut up.

326
00:22:33,351 --> 00:22:34,436
‪Shut up.

327
00:22:36,104 --> 00:22:37,397
‪Do you even know me?

328
00:22:37,481 --> 00:22:40,233
‪What do you even know about me
‪to say something like that?

329
00:22:41,526 --> 00:22:44,362
‪That only happened two months ago, right?

330
00:22:44,446 --> 00:22:46,073
‪Right. Two…

331
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:49,618
‪Two months ago was when…

332
00:22:49,701 --> 00:22:51,828
‪Oh, that was when we hit
‪a cooling-off period.

333
00:22:51,912 --> 00:22:53,914
‪-I see.
‪-Things were rocky then.

334
00:22:53,997 --> 00:22:56,541
‪Gosh, no. He didn't know her at all.

335
00:22:56,625 --> 00:22:57,834
‪Hey, I'm pleading the Fifth.

336
00:22:57,918 --> 00:22:59,419
‪-Yeah, sure.
‪-Cheers.

337
00:22:59,503 --> 00:23:02,047
‪Fine. Okay then. Next.

338
00:23:02,130 --> 00:23:04,341
‪"Next"? What more is there?

339
00:23:04,424 --> 00:23:06,676
‪"Calling me 'skin-deep'?"

340
00:23:07,260 --> 00:23:08,720
<i>‪And why should I know her?</i>

341
00:23:08,804 --> 00:23:10,430
‪I could say the same about her.

342
00:23:10,514 --> 00:23:14,726
‪Besides, why not drink on her own at home
‪instead of reserving half the diner?

343
00:23:14,810 --> 00:23:16,645
‪She calls herself the CEO of a hotel,

344
00:23:16,728 --> 00:23:18,814
‪yet she pulls
‪a drunken stunt like that in public?

345
00:23:19,481 --> 00:23:23,110
‪You were dating her at the time,
‪yet you chewed her out in private

346
00:23:23,193 --> 00:23:24,820
‪-in that scathing manner?
‪-Well…

347
00:23:25,403 --> 00:23:26,613
‪At the time…

348
00:23:27,239 --> 00:23:28,281
‪Back then…

349
00:23:29,407 --> 00:23:31,368
‪I had my reasons for that.

350
00:23:31,451 --> 00:23:33,954
‪You know couples have those rocky times.

351
00:23:34,579 --> 00:23:36,289
‪Besides, I thought
‪you didn't hear a word I said.

352
00:23:37,415 --> 00:23:39,501
‪-What?
‪-I don't believe you.

353
00:23:39,584 --> 00:23:42,212
‪-What did I do? Back then--
‪-You did me dirty.

354
00:23:42,295 --> 00:23:43,421
‪-Drink.
‪-Okay.

355
00:23:43,505 --> 00:23:46,216
‪Let's drink like crazy
‪and forget about everything.

356
00:23:52,139 --> 00:23:54,099
‪What? Do you have something to say?

357
00:23:54,975 --> 00:23:59,813
‪Well, if we're to assist you
‪to the best of our abilities,

358
00:23:59,896 --> 00:24:05,902
‪we need to know at least the basic facts
‪necessary to cover for you.

359
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:07,654
‪What do you mean, "cover for me"?

360
00:24:07,737 --> 00:24:10,323
‪Ms. Eom and I both think

361
00:24:10,407 --> 00:24:13,952
‪the chairwoman's excessive pressure
‪for you to get engaged made you fake…

362
00:24:15,328 --> 00:24:17,789
‪I mean, made you pretend to be engaged.

363
00:24:17,873 --> 00:24:19,416
‪"Pretend"?

364
00:24:20,625 --> 00:24:23,795
‪What do you mean, "pretend"?
‪Why would you say that?

365
00:24:23,879 --> 00:24:28,633
‪The premise that you dated for six months

366
00:24:28,717 --> 00:24:30,218
‪seems to be a bit of a stretch.

367
00:24:30,302 --> 00:24:32,888
‪I assist you in all matters, ma'am,

368
00:24:32,971 --> 00:24:36,558
‪and I say this because
‪we must be prepared for external attacks.

369
00:24:37,184 --> 00:24:38,476
‪I think it was two months ago.

370
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:40,228
‪I'm Ms. Cheon's executive secretary.

371
00:24:40,312 --> 00:24:42,063
‪Ms. Cheon isn't in at the moment.

372
00:24:44,024 --> 00:24:45,901
‪She sent this to me today.

373
00:24:46,484 --> 00:24:48,028
‪If you're her secretary,
‪pass it to her for me.

374
00:24:48,528 --> 00:24:50,780
‪He spoke as if he didn't know you.

375
00:24:54,492 --> 00:24:55,535
‪Well, back then…

376
00:24:59,080 --> 00:25:00,207
‪I was playing hard to get.

377
00:25:02,459 --> 00:25:07,088
‪We'd been flirting for a long time,
‪and things had gotten boring.

378
00:25:07,172 --> 00:25:09,382
‪I guess I wanted to get him worked up.

379
00:25:09,466 --> 00:25:11,843
‪-Oh, get him worked up?
‪-Yes, worked up.

380
00:25:11,927 --> 00:25:14,596
‪That's why I gifted him the shirt.

381
00:25:14,679 --> 00:25:17,849
‪His excuse of returning the shirt to me

382
00:25:18,433 --> 00:25:19,351
‪advanced our relationship.

383
00:25:19,434 --> 00:25:21,770
‪But if you dated him for six months

384
00:25:21,853 --> 00:25:24,314
‪and you played hard to get
‪until two months ago,

385
00:25:24,397 --> 00:25:27,025
‪-then your actual relationship began…
‪-Is that a problem?

386
00:25:27,609 --> 00:25:30,570
‪Are we not allowed to count
‪playing hard to get as dating?

387
00:25:32,489 --> 00:25:33,406
‪PROSECUTOR MA

388
00:25:34,699 --> 00:25:36,368
‪Oh, gosh. Hello?

389
00:25:38,328 --> 00:25:39,371
‪Hey, darling.

390
00:25:45,961 --> 00:25:49,172
‪Why did she leave when we should've left?

391
00:25:49,839 --> 00:25:51,758
‪She seemed quite flustered.

392
00:25:54,094 --> 00:25:54,970
‪Hello?

393
00:25:56,596 --> 00:25:57,973
‪That "darling" threw you off, didn't it?

394
00:25:58,807 --> 00:26:02,769
‪Yes, well, if you ask me,
‪I was quite startled.

395
00:26:05,855 --> 00:26:06,815
‪Isn't this Ma?

396
00:26:06,898 --> 00:26:09,526
‪Oh, right.

397
00:26:09,609 --> 00:26:13,280
‪We met once before. I'm Ko Pil-dong.

398
00:26:13,363 --> 00:26:14,614
<i>‪Hello, Ms. Cheon.</i>

399
00:26:14,698 --> 00:26:15,532
‪Oh, gosh.

400
00:26:16,616 --> 00:26:17,534
‪Hello.

401
00:26:19,995 --> 00:26:21,162
‪So where's Ma?

402
00:26:34,551 --> 00:26:36,970
‪-Your darling is…
‪-Yeo-ri.

403
00:26:39,306 --> 00:26:40,557
‪Yeo-ri…

404
00:26:41,266 --> 00:26:43,852
‪Ms. Cheon, this is the state
‪your darling is in.

405
00:26:53,111 --> 00:26:55,280
‪Excuse me, Investigator Ko.

406
00:26:56,197 --> 00:26:59,826
‪Ma's neck looks a bit uncomfortable.

407
00:27:00,452 --> 00:27:03,163
‪-Oh, his neck.
‪-Could you straighten him up?

408
00:27:06,583 --> 00:27:10,628
‪Is his hand wedged between the seats?

409
00:27:10,712 --> 00:27:12,464
‪-Wouldn't it get cramped?
‪-His hand?

410
00:27:12,547 --> 00:27:14,382
‪-You can see that?
‪-Yes.

411
00:27:14,924 --> 00:27:15,884
‪Hold on.

412
00:27:17,719 --> 00:27:20,764
‪It's okay. It's fine.

413
00:27:20,847 --> 00:27:23,141
‪-You're okay.
‪-It must've gone numb.

414
00:27:24,225 --> 00:27:27,354
‪Don't you think
‪he'd feel a bit suffocated?

415
00:27:27,437 --> 00:27:29,606
‪-His tie needs some loosening.
‪-Right, his tie.

416
00:27:30,857 --> 00:27:32,901
‪I think it's loose enough,
‪but just in case…

417
00:27:32,984 --> 00:27:34,486
‪-Yes, just in case.
‪-Got it.

418
00:27:35,445 --> 00:27:37,906
‪Here you go.

419
00:27:37,989 --> 00:27:40,700
‪That's better. He's all good now.

420
00:27:40,784 --> 00:27:44,204
‪-And--
‪-Yes? What is it now?

421
00:27:44,287 --> 00:27:46,831
‪Are you all right, Investigator Ko?

422
00:27:48,958 --> 00:27:51,211
‪-If you could stop ordering me around…
‪-Okay.

423
00:27:58,468 --> 00:28:00,637
‪-Thank you for driving us.
‪-Sure.

424
00:28:03,973 --> 00:28:04,933
‪Yeo-ri.

425
00:28:07,268 --> 00:28:09,479
‪-Let's see…
‪-I'll take that.

426
00:28:09,562 --> 00:28:11,856
‪-Sure. Thank you.
‪-Okay.

427
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:13,817
‪-Gang-uk.
‪-What?

428
00:28:13,900 --> 00:28:16,653
‪Come along. Yeah, there we go.

429
00:28:18,071 --> 00:28:19,614
‪Come with me, buddy.

430
00:28:19,697 --> 00:28:22,492
‪-Please watch his head.
‪-Okay.

431
00:28:23,118 --> 00:28:24,577
‪Come along, now.

432
00:28:27,080 --> 00:28:29,040
‪-Ms. Cheon.
‪-Yes?

433
00:28:29,124 --> 00:28:32,210
‪Can you get the gate key
‪from his briefcase?

434
00:28:32,293 --> 00:28:34,754
‪-Is it in here?
‪-Yes.

435
00:28:34,838 --> 00:28:36,673
‪Can you be quick?

436
00:28:36,756 --> 00:28:38,007
‪I don't think it's in here.

437
00:28:38,091 --> 00:28:39,634
‪Then check his pockets.

438
00:28:39,717 --> 00:28:43,096
‪-Can you go through his pockets?
‪-His pockets?

439
00:28:43,179 --> 00:28:46,224
‪-Yes, quickly.
‪-His pant pockets?

440
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:50,353
‪What if I climb over the wall instead?

441
00:28:50,437 --> 00:28:52,647
‪You'll climb the wall? Then I'll just…

442
00:28:57,402 --> 00:28:59,529
‪She can do that?

443
00:29:00,780 --> 00:29:02,282
‪I'll get the gate right away.

444
00:29:11,082 --> 00:29:12,333
‪Oh, no.

445
00:29:12,417 --> 00:29:15,044
‪Ma'am, you should've come to my place
‪if you had a favor to ask.

446
00:29:15,128 --> 00:29:16,838
‪Why did you come all the way here?

447
00:29:16,921 --> 00:29:17,964
‪Jeez.

448
00:29:18,465 --> 00:29:19,382
‪Who are you?

449
00:29:23,094 --> 00:29:24,012
‪Oh, my.

450
00:29:24,971 --> 00:29:26,014
‪You're human?

451
00:29:26,097 --> 00:29:28,808
‪Of course I'm human.
‪Do I look like a ghost to you?

452
00:29:29,684 --> 00:29:31,144
‪Who are you anyway?

453
00:29:31,227 --> 00:29:34,898
‪Why did you climb the wall
‪when there's a perfectly fine gate?

454
00:29:35,482 --> 00:29:37,317
‪Well, I…

455
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:39,986
‪The gate was locked,
‪so I needed to open it.

456
00:29:40,069 --> 00:29:40,904
‪I'm sorry.

457
00:29:45,325 --> 00:29:47,660
‪Oh, for goodness' sake.

458
00:29:48,620 --> 00:29:50,705
‪What's gotten into him now?

459
00:29:54,918 --> 00:29:58,087
‪-Oh, dear. Be careful.
‪-Okay.

460
00:29:58,171 --> 00:30:00,048
‪This fool of a boy…

461
00:30:00,131 --> 00:30:02,175
‪Oh, gosh. Get off him.

462
00:30:03,176 --> 00:30:04,385
‪Oh, goodness.

463
00:30:04,469 --> 00:30:06,012
‪Wake up, will you?

464
00:30:06,554 --> 00:30:10,141
‪Why did he drink so much?
‪He's completely out of it.

465
00:30:10,225 --> 00:30:12,477
‪Why didn't you stop him, Investigator Ko?

466
00:30:12,560 --> 00:30:14,103
‪You're older than him.

467
00:30:14,187 --> 00:30:15,313
‪I'm sorry.

468
00:30:16,731 --> 00:30:17,982
‪You there. Wait.

469
00:30:19,317 --> 00:30:20,568
‪Stay for a chat with me.

470
00:30:22,612 --> 00:30:24,155
‪Do you mean me?

471
00:30:24,239 --> 00:30:26,491
‪Is there someone other than you?

472
00:31:00,358 --> 00:31:01,776
‪Have some tea.

473
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:03,653
‪Yes. Thank you.

474
00:31:06,072 --> 00:31:09,200
‪I'm not sure if I should ask this
‪when we've just met,

475
00:31:10,118 --> 00:31:13,371
‪but are you and Gang-uk dating?

476
00:31:16,082 --> 00:31:18,501
‪I'm sorry if you're not.

477
00:31:18,585 --> 00:31:20,044
‪I'm old and out of touch.

478
00:31:20,128 --> 00:31:22,630
‪Seeing how you dropped him off
‪so late at night,

479
00:31:22,714 --> 00:31:25,258
‪I assumed you two were close.

480
00:31:27,719 --> 00:31:29,012
‪It's true that

481
00:31:29,888 --> 00:31:31,222
‪we're close.

482
00:31:31,890 --> 00:31:33,057
‪So you <i>‪are</i>‪ close?

483
00:31:36,644 --> 00:31:37,520
‪I'm so thirsty.

484
00:31:37,604 --> 00:31:38,438
‪A bit?

485
00:31:39,606 --> 00:31:40,773
‪A lot?

486
00:31:41,566 --> 00:31:43,610
‪Quite a lot, I guess?

487
00:31:43,693 --> 00:31:46,154
‪Oh, quite a lot?

488
00:31:48,114 --> 00:31:51,075
‪So if you two are close,

489
00:31:51,159 --> 00:31:54,537
‪-Madam Pang?
‪-you could get even closer, right?

490
00:31:55,663 --> 00:31:57,790
‪-What's Yeo-ri doing here?
‪-Then

491
00:31:57,874 --> 00:32:01,210
‪I must ask you something else,

492
00:32:01,294 --> 00:32:04,547
‪since you never know
‪how things will turn out.

493
00:32:04,631 --> 00:32:07,759
‪Tell me, what's your zodiac sign?

494
00:32:07,842 --> 00:32:08,968
‪-Her zodiac sign?
‪-Sorry?

495
00:32:09,052 --> 00:32:10,887
‪I mean your birth year.

496
00:32:11,638 --> 00:32:12,889
‪My birth year?

497
00:32:13,431 --> 00:32:14,432
‪I was born in

498
00:32:16,392 --> 00:32:18,686
‪-the year of the mon--
‪-No!

499
00:32:20,521 --> 00:32:23,399
‪No, no! Don't!

500
00:32:23,483 --> 00:32:25,151
‪No!

501
00:32:25,234 --> 00:32:27,779
‪-What's gotten into you?
‪-No.

502
00:32:27,862 --> 00:32:29,656
‪-What's going on?
‪-Ice water.

503
00:32:29,739 --> 00:32:32,909
‪-I'm thirsty.
‪-Oh, you're thirsty?

504
00:32:35,912 --> 00:32:37,664
‪No, I'll see her off.

505
00:32:38,164 --> 00:32:41,501
‪Why won't you let me
‪see off a guest in my home?

506
00:32:41,584 --> 00:32:42,710
‪Will you stop it?

507
00:32:42,794 --> 00:32:44,963
‪How is this your house, Grandma?

508
00:32:45,046 --> 00:32:47,757
‪I own it jointly with the bank
‪that gave me the mortgage.

509
00:32:47,840 --> 00:32:49,258
‪-Go back inside.
‪-Wait…

510
00:32:49,342 --> 00:32:50,969
‪-Let me--
‪-All right, go inside.

511
00:32:51,052 --> 00:32:52,512
‪-Let me see her off--
‪-Whatever!

512
00:32:52,595 --> 00:32:55,598
‪-I want to see her off!
‪-No, I'm closing the door.

513
00:32:56,891 --> 00:32:58,101
‪Oh, my head hurts.

514
00:33:01,646 --> 00:33:02,730
‪Yeo-ri.

515
00:33:03,564 --> 00:33:06,192
‪I'm sorry I caused you so much trouble.

516
00:33:06,776 --> 00:33:07,944
‪No, not at all.

517
00:33:08,444 --> 00:33:12,615
‪Your grandmother asked me
‪what our relationship was like,

518
00:33:13,324 --> 00:33:17,078
‪so I just told her
‪we were kind of close, just in case.

519
00:33:17,161 --> 00:33:18,830
‪Yeah, good call.

520
00:33:19,455 --> 00:33:23,001
‪I haven't told her anything yet,
‪so things could've gotten out of hand.

521
00:33:23,960 --> 00:33:26,295
‪She also asked about my Chinese zodiac,

522
00:33:26,379 --> 00:33:28,297
‪but I didn't get to answer her.

523
00:33:28,381 --> 00:33:30,508
‪I was born in the year of the monkey.

524
00:33:30,591 --> 00:33:33,428
‪-You can tell her for me.
‪-Sure.

525
00:33:35,430 --> 00:33:36,472
‪The thing is,

526
00:33:37,265 --> 00:33:39,434
‪I don't think anyone believes us.

527
00:33:39,517 --> 00:33:41,644
‪Why don't we actually make some proof?

528
00:33:43,021 --> 00:33:43,855
‪Proof?

529
00:33:43,938 --> 00:33:44,772
‪Yeah.

530
00:33:48,359 --> 00:33:49,360
‪Man…

531
00:33:53,614 --> 00:33:55,158
‪-Shall we?
‪-Sure.

532
00:33:55,241 --> 00:33:56,576
‪Look at all these options.

533
00:33:56,659 --> 00:33:57,785
‪Should I get you a stuffed toy?

534
00:33:59,370 --> 00:34:00,246
‪Grab it by the ear.

535
00:34:04,542 --> 00:34:05,960
‪Oh, darn it.

536
00:34:06,044 --> 00:34:06,919
‪That was a warm-up.

537
00:34:08,129 --> 00:34:09,297
‪Here goes.

538
00:34:23,853 --> 00:34:24,937
‪Can I give it a try?

539
00:34:25,021 --> 00:34:27,023
‪Sure. It won't be easy though.

540
00:34:37,116 --> 00:34:38,117
‪No way.

541
00:34:48,044 --> 00:34:50,296
‪These parts should come together
‪to form a ring.

542
00:34:50,379 --> 00:34:51,839
‪You nailed the posture.

543
00:34:55,426 --> 00:34:56,636
‪What's going on?

544
00:35:01,182 --> 00:35:02,350
‪Where's the plushie?

545
00:35:10,274 --> 00:35:12,568
‪You're not too bad at basketball, Gang-uk.

546
00:35:25,665 --> 00:35:26,916
‪Are you in first place?

547
00:35:34,340 --> 00:35:37,051
‪-Yeo-ri, we have to pick a pose.
‪-Okay.

548
00:35:37,635 --> 00:35:39,011
‪I'd say the standard one is…

549
00:35:42,723 --> 00:35:43,558
‪Let's make a heart.

550
00:35:46,894 --> 00:35:49,730
‪-Next, let's take the glasses off.
‪-The glasses?

551
00:35:49,814 --> 00:35:52,817
‪-Look straight at the camera.
‪-At the camera? Okay.

552
00:36:05,454 --> 00:36:07,039
‪I kept you waiting, didn't I? Sorry.

553
00:36:07,123 --> 00:36:08,749
‪It's fine. I just stepped out.

554
00:36:10,084 --> 00:36:11,210
‪Next on the agenda

555
00:36:11,294 --> 00:36:13,963
‪is sharing hobbies,
‪and I'll share mine first.

556
00:36:15,464 --> 00:36:17,550
‪Show me jogging spots by the Han River.

557
00:36:18,342 --> 00:36:19,927
<i>‪Which option do you prefer?</i>

558
00:36:20,011 --> 00:36:21,095
‪The second one.

559
00:36:21,846 --> 00:36:22,847
‪Let's go.

560
00:36:25,850 --> 00:36:28,895
‪Man, the weather's awesome today.

561
00:36:28,978 --> 00:36:30,396
‪You said you go to the river often.

562
00:36:30,479 --> 00:36:32,815
‪Yeah, all the time.
‪I often go in the mornings.

563
00:36:32,899 --> 00:36:35,276
‪-For your hangover <i>‪ramyeon?</i>
‪-Well, that's…

564
00:36:42,325 --> 00:36:44,243
‪Look, <i>‪ramyeon.</i>

565
00:36:48,456 --> 00:36:50,041
‪-Oh, wait.
‪-What?

566
00:36:51,500 --> 00:36:52,335
‪A selfie.

567
00:36:55,213 --> 00:36:57,381
‪-All right, to the next spot.
‪-The next one?

568
00:36:57,465 --> 00:36:58,341
‪Hurry up.

569
00:37:05,348 --> 00:37:07,808
‪How strong is her grip?
‪She makes it look so easy.

570
00:37:14,857 --> 00:37:16,734
‪Wow, that was awesome.

571
00:37:16,817 --> 00:37:17,652
‪It's your turn now.

572
00:37:17,735 --> 00:37:19,278
‪-What?
‪-Go on.

573
00:37:19,779 --> 00:37:22,073
‪I've tried pretty much every sport,

574
00:37:22,156 --> 00:37:24,450
‪but this is my first time
‪doing indoor rock climbing…

575
00:37:25,076 --> 00:37:25,910
‪Okay.

576
00:37:25,993 --> 00:37:27,578
‪Be careful. It's harder than you think.

577
00:37:28,120 --> 00:37:29,872
‪One foot right here.

578
00:37:29,956 --> 00:37:31,415
‪-Take it slow.
‪-Watch me.

579
00:37:32,458 --> 00:37:34,335
‪What's next? Where does my other foot go?

580
00:37:34,418 --> 00:37:36,045
‪On that red one. One,

581
00:37:36,963 --> 00:37:38,256
‪-two,
‪-Two,

582
00:37:38,339 --> 00:37:39,507
‪-three.
‪-Three!

583
00:38:32,768 --> 00:38:33,853
‪Yes, Mr. Bong.

584
00:38:34,520 --> 00:38:35,479
<i>‪Ms. Cheon.</i>

585
00:38:36,188 --> 00:38:40,234
<i>‪I've looked into</i>
<i>‪what </i><i>‪you </i><i>‪instructed </i><i>‪in </i><i>‪secret.</i>

586
00:38:40,318 --> 00:38:41,777
<i>‪When would you like to be briefed?</i>

587
00:38:42,570 --> 00:38:43,654
‪Oh, about that.

588
00:38:51,871 --> 00:38:55,499
‪Those are the details of the artworks
‪we've purchased over the past ten years.

589
00:38:55,583 --> 00:39:01,964
‪Over 40% were pieces by rising artists
‪that we paid above market value for.

590
00:39:03,966 --> 00:39:07,511
‪The head of the Art Team that you replaced
‪when you took over as CEO

591
00:39:07,595 --> 00:39:11,474
‪moved to Gallery Cheon
‪and has been working there since.

592
00:39:12,558 --> 00:39:14,477
‪-Head of Audit, anything to add?
‪-Right.

593
00:39:21,776 --> 00:39:23,361
‪Five years ago, Gallery Cheon owned

594
00:39:23,444 --> 00:39:25,821
‪four pieces by Linaldo Rosy
‪including "Untitled."

595
00:39:25,905 --> 00:39:27,490
‪Reina Resort's director, Cheon Dong-jun…

596
00:39:27,573 --> 00:39:30,201
‪He falsely claimed
‪they were his personal collection

597
00:39:30,868 --> 00:39:32,370
‪and took out a loan against them?

598
00:39:32,453 --> 00:39:33,412
‪Yes.

599
00:39:33,913 --> 00:39:35,664
‪How much was the loan in total?

600
00:39:35,748 --> 00:39:36,582
‪About 50 billion won.

601
00:39:39,335 --> 00:39:41,712
‪What do you plan to do?

602
00:39:43,798 --> 00:39:45,257
‪Even if we make this public,

603
00:39:45,341 --> 00:39:47,468
‪we'll need a contingency plan
‪put in place first.

604
00:39:48,677 --> 00:39:49,553
‪I'll think about it.

605
00:39:50,554 --> 00:39:52,765
‪Let's keep this under wraps for now.

606
00:39:53,265 --> 00:39:54,392
‪Understood.

607
00:39:55,893 --> 00:39:57,478
‪Oh, gosh. I'm a bit late, aren't I?

608
00:39:58,104 --> 00:40:00,731
‪I hope the trip here
‪wasn't too troublesome, Director Gong.

609
00:40:00,815 --> 00:40:03,275
‪Not at all. You even sent me a car.

610
00:40:03,359 --> 00:40:05,152
‪-I came over in great comfort.
‪-Good.

611
00:40:09,115 --> 00:40:12,535
‪What happened that evening
‪was a bit perplexing, wasn't it?

612
00:40:12,618 --> 00:40:15,788
‪What exactly is going on with Reina?

613
00:40:15,871 --> 00:40:17,832
‪And what's gotten into Ms. Cheon?

614
00:40:17,915 --> 00:40:20,418
‪Does she think getting engaged
‪is some kind of joke?

615
00:40:20,501 --> 00:40:25,172
‪I asked to see you
‪hoping we could discuss that very matter.

616
00:40:26,215 --> 00:40:29,760
‪Six years ago, when Yeo-ri broke off
‪her engagement with Cha & Yul,

617
00:40:29,844 --> 00:40:31,470
‪and the aftermath of it.

618
00:40:32,638 --> 00:40:33,848
‪You remember, don't you?

619
00:40:35,224 --> 00:40:36,684
‪6 YEARS AGO

620
00:40:36,767 --> 00:40:38,769
‪We're here today

621
00:40:38,853 --> 00:40:42,314
‪to convey our view on who'd be
‪best suited as Reina Hotel's CEO.

622
00:40:42,398 --> 00:40:43,649
‪We'd strongly prefer

623
00:40:43,732 --> 00:40:47,736
‪Director Cheon Dong-jun of Reina Resorts
‪to oversee both businesses,

624
00:40:47,820 --> 00:40:50,197
‪rather than Director Cheon Yeo-ri.

625
00:40:50,823 --> 00:40:52,741
‪Appointing Ms. Cheon
‪as Reina Hotel's new CEO

626
00:40:52,825 --> 00:40:55,953
‪seems like an irrational choice
‪based on blood and favoritism.

627
00:40:56,036 --> 00:40:59,081
‪Isn't Director Cheon Dong-jun
‪also my bloodline?

628
00:40:59,165 --> 00:41:04,962
‪It's uncomfortable to bring this up
‪when she's here with us,

629
00:41:05,045 --> 00:41:09,508
‪but the broken engagement
‪did a lot of damage to Reina's reputation,

630
00:41:09,592 --> 00:41:11,844
‪and our stock prices took a hit.

631
00:41:11,927 --> 00:41:15,389
‪We think it's best
‪that she keeps her head down--

632
00:41:15,473 --> 00:41:16,307
‪Wait.

633
00:41:18,184 --> 00:41:20,561
‪Telling me to keep my head down
‪when I didn't do anything

634
00:41:20,644 --> 00:41:21,979
‪I should be criticized for?

635
00:41:22,855 --> 00:41:24,523
‪Please mind your language.

636
00:41:26,484 --> 00:41:29,445
‪After all, it was Cha Gi-u
‪who didn't show up

637
00:41:29,528 --> 00:41:31,405
‪to his own engagement ceremony.

638
00:41:31,489 --> 00:41:35,159
‪The reasonable conclusion is
‪that the liability lies with him.

639
00:41:36,076 --> 00:41:37,119
‪Don't you think?

640
00:41:37,203 --> 00:41:40,039
‪It's very clear to me
‪where you all stand, Directors.

641
00:41:40,748 --> 00:41:43,876
‪All we can do now
‪is to settle it with a vote.

642
00:41:45,252 --> 00:41:46,504
‪I'll see you at the general meeting.

643
00:41:47,046 --> 00:41:48,881
<i>‪I believe that back then, Ms. Cheon</i>

644
00:41:48,964 --> 00:41:53,385
‪took us head-on at the general meeting
‪and that was the end of it.

645
00:41:53,969 --> 00:41:55,471
‪Yes, that's what happened then.

646
00:41:56,847 --> 00:42:00,601
‪But recently,
‪there have been unsettling rumors…

647
00:42:03,145 --> 00:42:08,817
‪recirculating about Cheon Yeo-ri
‪being a shaman who sees ghosts.

648
00:42:13,572 --> 00:42:18,118
‪These are the recordings and proof
‪we collected about the rumors.

649
00:42:18,202 --> 00:42:19,328
‪Take a look.

650
00:42:19,411 --> 00:42:22,039
‪If you think this is a serious matter,

651
00:42:23,123 --> 00:42:25,417
‪shouldn't we arrange a meeting

652
00:42:25,501 --> 00:42:28,337
‪with the directors
‪who served under the former chairman?

653
00:42:28,921 --> 00:42:32,967
‪Perhaps you could also voice your concerns
‪to Chairwoman Baek

654
00:42:33,467 --> 00:42:37,346
‪about CEO Cheon Yeo-ri
‪and the risk she brings to Reina.

655
00:42:40,432 --> 00:42:41,976
‪-Hello, Chairwoman.
<i>‪-Hey.</i>

656
00:42:42,059 --> 00:42:44,770
‪Come and see me tomorrow
‪with Prosecutor Ma.

657
00:42:45,896 --> 00:42:46,814
‪What?

658
00:42:49,275 --> 00:42:51,527
‪Hey, it's supposed to rain
‪on this week's sports day.

659
00:42:51,610 --> 00:42:53,320
‪We can't cancel
‪the catered lunch order, can we?

660
00:42:53,404 --> 00:42:54,363
‪CEO CHEON YEO-RI

661
00:42:54,446 --> 00:42:56,740
‪-I guess that's…
‪-Hello?

662
00:42:58,158 --> 00:42:59,493
‪Why did he even ask?

663
00:43:00,077 --> 00:43:01,870
‪The chairwoman? Tomorrow?

664
00:43:03,455 --> 00:43:04,915
‪It's fine. I'll be there.

665
00:43:09,461 --> 00:43:12,339
‪You'll hear about it anyway,
‪so you might as well listen in.

666
00:43:13,090 --> 00:43:13,924
‪Okay.

667
00:43:14,008 --> 00:43:15,968
‪I got a call yesterday.

668
00:43:16,051 --> 00:43:21,140
‪Director Gong wants me to arrange
‪a meeting with you and Prosecutor Ma.

669
00:43:22,266 --> 00:43:23,892
‪It looks like Director Ok

670
00:43:23,976 --> 00:43:26,604
‪is taking actual steps
‪to keep you in check.

671
00:43:26,687 --> 00:43:30,899
‪I assumed as much when I saw
‪she'd invited Director Gong to dinner.

672
00:43:30,983 --> 00:43:34,361
‪She must be trying to win over
‪the late chairman's loyalists

673
00:43:34,445 --> 00:43:35,696
‪who can cast the deciding votes.

674
00:43:37,281 --> 00:43:41,702
‪If Director Ok is behind this,
‪there will be an ulterior motive.

675
00:43:42,828 --> 00:43:44,455
‪I am prepared in my own way.

676
00:43:45,789 --> 00:43:47,374
‪Will you be okay with a meeting like this?

677
00:43:48,792 --> 00:43:49,918
‪Of course I'll be okay.

678
00:43:50,544 --> 00:43:51,712
‪It's no trouble for me at all.

679
00:43:53,672 --> 00:43:54,548
‪Ma'am.

680
00:43:58,093 --> 00:44:01,513
‪There's a decision I made
‪after meeting Yeo-ri.

681
00:44:02,723 --> 00:44:04,308
‪It's that when she's struggling,

682
00:44:04,975 --> 00:44:06,685
‪I'll never let her go through it alone.

683
00:44:07,394 --> 00:44:10,105
‪No matter where she is or where I am,

684
00:44:12,066 --> 00:44:13,484
‪I'll be there by her side.

685
00:44:34,004 --> 00:44:35,130
‪Why did you want to see me?

686
00:44:35,839 --> 00:44:38,133
‪You sounded so confident last time,

687
00:44:38,926 --> 00:44:41,136
‪but Prosecutor Ma's already here
‪speaking with the chairwoman.

688
00:44:42,471 --> 00:44:44,098
‪They're ready to get engaged any day now.

689
00:44:47,309 --> 00:44:49,687
‪You asked me to come
‪all this way to tell me that?

690
00:44:49,770 --> 00:44:51,188
‪You said you haven't
‪given up on Yeo-ri yet.

691
00:44:52,314 --> 00:44:55,234
‪My mom and brother are putting
‪lots of pressure on them.

692
00:44:55,317 --> 00:44:58,237
‪They could set an engagement date
‪anytime to cover up the rumor.

693
00:44:59,863 --> 00:45:01,323
‪So I was thinking…

694
00:45:01,907 --> 00:45:03,117
‪Why don't we join forces?

695
00:45:04,034 --> 00:45:05,994
‪I know of a way to stop the engagement.

696
00:45:10,124 --> 00:45:13,210
‪Wouldn't it be better for you
‪if Yeo-ri were to marry Ma Gang-uk?

697
00:45:14,211 --> 00:45:16,255
‪We don't care that it's Ma Gang-uk.

698
00:45:16,880 --> 00:45:20,551
‪What we want is for Yeo-ri
‪not to get engaged for the time being.

699
00:45:20,634 --> 00:45:24,054
‪As you know,
‪our priority is to stall for time

700
00:45:24,138 --> 00:45:27,683
‪and prove in the meantime
‪that she's incapable of running a company.

701
00:45:29,977 --> 00:45:32,604
‪I've made my offer,
‪so you decide whether to take it.

702
00:45:33,188 --> 00:45:34,690
‪We must stop the engagement somehow.

703
00:45:48,579 --> 00:45:49,872
‪What is it?

704
00:45:49,955 --> 00:45:50,789
‪It's just…

705
00:45:51,707 --> 00:45:52,624
‪It's nothing.

706
00:45:53,917 --> 00:45:54,751
‪Let's go.

707
00:45:57,838 --> 00:45:59,006
‪Oh, sorry.

708
00:46:02,176 --> 00:46:05,345
‪You're so consistent
‪about keeping your distance.

709
00:46:08,557 --> 00:46:10,559
‪How come you treat everyone the same,

710
00:46:11,143 --> 00:46:13,395
‪whether they're your fiancé or your staff?

711
00:46:14,146 --> 00:46:15,898
‪What are you trying to say?

712
00:46:15,981 --> 00:46:16,857
‪I mean,

713
00:46:16,940 --> 00:46:20,861
‪you can usually spot a couple
‪just from the way they stand together.

714
00:46:20,944 --> 00:46:23,780
‪But you two were standing apart
‪as if you just fought.

715
00:46:23,864 --> 00:46:25,365
‪I was just asking

716
00:46:25,449 --> 00:46:29,328
‪in case news of your breakup is released
‪before the engagement is even announced.

717
00:46:30,162 --> 00:46:32,039
‪This hotel is where I work.

718
00:46:32,122 --> 00:46:35,918
‪Isn't it only natural and right
‪not to show affection in public?

719
00:46:36,001 --> 00:46:38,086
‪Why do you care so much
‪about what others think?

720
00:46:38,712 --> 00:46:41,131
‪You should be blinded
‪if you're in love enough to get engaged.

721
00:46:41,215 --> 00:46:42,341
‪They say

722
00:46:43,467 --> 00:46:44,718
‪deep waters make no noise.

723
00:46:46,637 --> 00:46:47,554
‪-Is that so?
‪-Yes.

724
00:46:47,638 --> 00:46:49,515
‪What are your plans for this weekend?

725
00:46:49,598 --> 00:46:51,058
‪-A meeting.
‪-A family sports day.

726
00:46:54,269 --> 00:46:55,437
‪A "family" sports day?

727
00:46:55,521 --> 00:46:58,440
‪You're attending a sports day event
‪as a prosecutor's family member?

728
00:46:58,524 --> 00:47:00,359
‪What I meant to say was

729
00:47:00,442 --> 00:47:02,945
‪she was going to attend the sports day,

730
00:47:03,028 --> 00:47:04,530
‪but since she has a meeting,

731
00:47:04,613 --> 00:47:06,615
‪I'd decided to go on my own.

732
00:47:07,241 --> 00:47:08,867
‪If it weren't for the weekend conference,

733
00:47:08,951 --> 00:47:10,994
‪I'd have liked to go and watch.
‪It's a shame.

734
00:47:11,078 --> 00:47:11,995
‪It is.

735
00:47:12,496 --> 00:47:14,998
‪I meant to inform you of that, Ms. Cheon.

736
00:47:15,082 --> 00:47:18,335
‪The women entrepreneurs' conference
‪has been postponed to next week.

737
00:47:18,961 --> 00:47:20,087
‪What?

738
00:47:20,170 --> 00:47:22,339
‪That means you can go and have fun.

739
00:47:23,465 --> 00:47:26,343
‪-Why was it postponed?
‪-I'm not sure…

740
00:47:26,426 --> 00:47:28,387
‪-Should I look into it?
‪-Excuse us.

741
00:47:29,221 --> 00:47:30,305
‪Goodbye then.

742
00:47:34,726 --> 00:47:35,852
‪I can't wait

743
00:47:36,353 --> 00:47:38,230
‪for the prosecutors' family sports day.

744
00:47:41,567 --> 00:47:43,610
‪What's this about the sports day?

745
00:47:44,528 --> 00:47:47,072
‪The sports day isn't the problem.

746
00:47:47,155 --> 00:47:48,740
‪I'm concerned your plan was canceled.

747
00:47:48,824 --> 00:47:50,450
‪Why'd it have to get canceled now?

748
00:47:51,994 --> 00:47:54,037
‪It was postponed, not canceled.

749
00:47:54,121 --> 00:47:57,124
‪Also, you should've told me
‪if there was an event like that.

750
00:47:59,126 --> 00:48:00,043
‪I'm sorry.

751
00:48:01,003 --> 00:48:02,421
‪They suspect us, don't they?

752
00:48:03,505 --> 00:48:05,799
‪Ha-ri will never believe-- Oh, jeez.

753
00:48:07,050 --> 00:48:09,928
‪She always doubts and suspects,
‪and she's persistent too.

754
00:48:11,096 --> 00:48:11,930
‪Hey, Hyeong-min.

755
00:48:12,514 --> 00:48:15,726
‪Mr. Ma. The sports day's been canceled
‪because of the rain forecast.

756
00:48:15,809 --> 00:48:17,978
<i>‪-There's a team dinner instead.</i>
‪-Really?

757
00:48:18,687 --> 00:48:19,521
<i>‪Yes, really.</i>

758
00:48:19,605 --> 00:48:20,647
‪Okay, thanks.

759
00:48:22,399 --> 00:48:25,485
‪Yeo-ri, they canceled sports day
‪because of the rain forecast.

760
00:48:28,030 --> 00:48:29,948
‪Be more careful from now on.

761
00:48:30,032 --> 00:48:30,866
‪Okay.

762
00:48:30,949 --> 00:48:31,908
‪Shall we?

763
00:48:34,661 --> 00:48:36,455
‪As for Fiel Seoul,

764
00:48:36,538 --> 00:48:38,874
‪the basic investment is 30.5 billion won,

765
00:48:38,957 --> 00:48:40,792
‪and the extra investment
‪is one billion won.

766
00:48:40,876 --> 00:48:43,503
‪The total price of underwriting
‪is 31.5 billion won.

767
00:48:43,587 --> 00:48:47,049
‪On top of that, we're taking on
‪the resort's debt of 400 billion won.

768
00:48:47,591 --> 00:48:49,509
‪That means our total bill
‪is 431.5 billion won.

769
00:48:56,058 --> 00:48:57,809
‪Let's confirm the deal and wrap things up.

770
00:48:58,435 --> 00:48:59,770
‪-Yes, sir.
‪-Great work.

771
00:48:59,853 --> 00:49:01,605
‪-Good job.
‪-Good work, sir.

772
00:49:03,023 --> 00:49:03,857
‪Oh, right.

773
00:49:06,943 --> 00:49:09,529
‪You all worked hard doing overtime,

774
00:49:10,030 --> 00:49:11,948
‪and we still have other projects.

775
00:49:12,032 --> 00:49:13,533
‪-I got you an energy booster.
‪-Red ginseng?

776
00:49:14,451 --> 00:49:15,327
‪Thank you.

777
00:49:15,410 --> 00:49:17,913
‪-Thank you, sir.
‪-Save energy for when you need it next.

778
00:49:18,497 --> 00:49:19,331
‪Take one each.

779
00:49:21,291 --> 00:49:22,417
‪You first, sir.

780
00:49:23,669 --> 00:49:24,836
‪-Thank you.
‪-Of course.

781
00:49:28,965 --> 00:49:29,925
‪Mr. Kang.

782
00:49:30,008 --> 00:49:31,927
‪About the task you gave me last time,

783
00:49:32,010 --> 00:49:33,512
‪I'll send you what I have right now.

784
00:50:00,664 --> 00:50:06,211
‪12 YEARS AGO

785
00:50:19,391 --> 00:50:21,143
‪Min-hwan. Are you busy?

786
00:50:21,226 --> 00:50:22,728
‪No, not really.

787
00:50:23,311 --> 00:50:24,146
‪What is it?

788
00:50:26,314 --> 00:50:27,357
‪What do you think of these?

789
00:50:32,154 --> 00:50:32,988
‪What are these?

790
00:50:33,071 --> 00:50:34,740
‪They're for Yeo-ri and me.

791
00:50:34,823 --> 00:50:37,367
‪I'm going to give one to her
‪on our trip soon.

792
00:50:40,954 --> 00:50:43,290
‪What's wrong? Is it too much?

793
00:50:44,541 --> 00:50:45,542
‪Did you

794
00:50:46,334 --> 00:50:47,294
‪ask her out already?

795
00:50:47,377 --> 00:50:48,420
‪No, not yet.

796
00:50:50,255 --> 00:50:51,840
‪Would matching rings be too much?

797
00:50:54,593 --> 00:50:55,886
‪It would make her feel uncomfortable.

798
00:50:56,678 --> 00:50:58,013
‪You've been friends since childhood.

799
00:50:58,805 --> 00:51:00,140
‪What should I do?

800
00:51:00,223 --> 00:51:03,351
‪Should I give her something else,
‪like earrings or a necklace?

801
00:51:04,519 --> 00:51:07,439
‪Yeah, I think that would be better.

802
00:51:07,522 --> 00:51:10,025
‪Right? Thanks, bro.

803
00:51:10,108 --> 00:51:11,067
‪Sure.

804
00:51:37,969 --> 00:51:38,970
‪DISTRICT CHIEF PROSECUTOR

805
00:51:42,390 --> 00:51:43,433
‪Hello. It's been a while.

806
00:51:44,851 --> 00:51:46,436
‪I have business
‪near your Seocho-dong office.

807
00:51:47,020 --> 00:51:49,439
‪Will you buy me some tea if I visit?

808
00:51:57,739 --> 00:51:59,533
‪Can we eat something else next?

809
00:51:59,616 --> 00:52:01,618
‪Why? Soup and rice are nice and hot.

810
00:52:01,701 --> 00:52:02,744
‪-Huh?
‪-It should've been my treat.

811
00:52:02,828 --> 00:52:04,371
‪Does it matter who buys?

812
00:52:04,454 --> 00:52:06,790
‪-The District Chief Prosecutor?
‪-It'll be my treat.

813
00:52:06,873 --> 00:52:08,041
‪What's the matter?

814
00:52:08,124 --> 00:52:09,960
‪The personnel shuffle is coming up.

815
00:52:10,043 --> 00:52:12,504
‪I need to get on his radar when I can.

816
00:52:12,587 --> 00:52:13,880
‪Oh, jeez.

817
00:52:15,173 --> 00:52:17,175
‪Hello, sir. Did you have lunch?

818
00:52:17,259 --> 00:52:19,636
‪-Mr. Nam. Is everything good?
‪-Yes, sir.

819
00:52:20,178 --> 00:52:22,389
‪Goodbye then, sir.
‪Thank you for the lunch.

820
00:52:22,472 --> 00:52:24,850
‪Sure thing, Mr. Kang. I'll see you around.

821
00:52:24,933 --> 00:52:26,017
‪-Yes, sir.
‪-I'll escort you, sir.

822
00:52:26,101 --> 00:52:28,144
‪-How are things?
‪-Good, sir.

823
00:52:28,228 --> 00:52:30,105
‪Man, it must be nice to be rich,

824
00:52:30,188 --> 00:52:31,857
‪seeing you're rich with connections too.

825
00:52:31,940 --> 00:52:35,652
‪You seem close to the organization's
‪second-most powerful man.

826
00:52:37,237 --> 00:52:39,114
‪Come to me if you need any favors.

827
00:52:39,197 --> 00:52:41,032
‪I'll put in a good word for you.

828
00:52:41,116 --> 00:52:43,159
‪That's called soliciting favors,
‪which I hate the most.

829
00:52:44,911 --> 00:52:47,330
‪My lunchtime is up,
‪so I should get back.

830
00:52:47,831 --> 00:52:51,293
‪Why don't you call off the engagement
‪while you can?

831
00:52:52,919 --> 00:52:53,837
‪Why should I do that?

832
00:52:53,920 --> 00:52:55,630
‪The conclusion is already drawn.

833
00:52:56,381 --> 00:52:58,508
‪You won't make it
‪to the engagement ceremony,

834
00:52:59,259 --> 00:53:00,802
‪and Yeo-ri will only get hurt again.

835
00:53:00,886 --> 00:53:01,970
‪So I'm saying…

836
00:53:04,097 --> 00:53:05,432
‪you should give up now.

837
00:53:07,976 --> 00:53:09,185
‪I don't believe this.

838
00:53:09,269 --> 00:53:12,939
‪How do you know a future I don't even know
‪and decide if I can make it or not?

839
00:53:13,023 --> 00:53:16,359
‪Are you not the head of CL Group,
‪but of a fortune-telling group too?

840
00:53:16,860 --> 00:53:19,571
‪If you're doing this
‪because you can't accept our engagement,

841
00:53:19,654 --> 00:53:21,156
‪you can skip the ceremony altogether.

842
00:53:21,239 --> 00:53:22,365
‪I'd totally understand.

843
00:53:23,408 --> 00:53:24,409
‪Jeez.

844
00:53:39,883 --> 00:53:43,595
‪CIVIL SERVANT PERSONNEL FILE

845
00:53:45,347 --> 00:53:47,432
‪SEOUL CENTRAL DISTRICT PROSECUTORS' OFFICE

846
00:53:57,859 --> 00:54:00,403
‪Are you sure Sio Atelier supplied these?

847
00:54:00,487 --> 00:54:02,280
‪Well…

848
00:54:04,282 --> 00:54:05,992
‪Yes, that is correct.

849
00:54:06,076 --> 00:54:07,827
‪Is there a problem?

850
00:54:08,703 --> 00:54:10,330
‪It's not Sio's usual style.

851
00:54:14,000 --> 00:54:15,710
‪3 WEEKS AGO

852
00:54:15,794 --> 00:54:16,795
‪That's a shame.

853
00:54:17,295 --> 00:54:20,215
‪You decorated the lobby
‪and all the suites.

854
00:54:20,298 --> 00:54:22,050
‪Sio Atelier did a perfect job.

855
00:54:22,884 --> 00:54:23,802
‪You don't mean that.

856
00:54:24,761 --> 00:54:27,305
‪I heard you're already
‪collaborating with Jane Müller.

857
00:54:27,847 --> 00:54:30,100
‪Müller is the best in the world,

858
00:54:31,017 --> 00:54:33,019
‪and it's the choice
‪I'd expect you to make.

859
00:54:33,103 --> 00:54:35,480
‪So why the sudden decision
‪to go on a trip?

860
00:54:36,523 --> 00:54:38,942
‪I wanted to keep you on
‪for the next season.

861
00:54:39,025 --> 00:54:40,527
‪I'm sorry, Ms. Cheon.

862
00:54:40,610 --> 00:54:42,487
‪I was too burned out,

863
00:54:42,570 --> 00:54:45,073
‪and I needed some time to recharge.

864
00:54:45,156 --> 00:54:49,327
‪The plan is to visit
‪about 40 countries in Europe.

865
00:54:49,911 --> 00:54:52,247
‪-When are you leaving?
‪-At the end of the month.

866
00:54:52,747 --> 00:54:54,791
‪Oh, and in case you're worried,

867
00:54:54,874 --> 00:54:57,377
‪I'll finish everything up for Reina
‪before I leave,

868
00:54:57,460 --> 00:54:59,254
‪so don't worry about that.

869
00:55:01,214 --> 00:55:02,799
‪When were the flowers replaced?

870
00:55:03,299 --> 00:55:06,219
‪They're delivered every Tuesday.
‪Some are set up right away,

871
00:55:06,302 --> 00:55:09,514
‪and some are kept in the fridge overnight
‪to be set out the following day.

872
00:55:10,473 --> 00:55:13,018
‪That means most of the flowers
‪were replaced on Wednesday.

873
00:55:13,852 --> 00:55:15,478
‪Didn't you notice anything wrong?

874
00:55:15,562 --> 00:55:16,479
‪I apologize.

875
00:55:16,563 --> 00:55:20,191
‪I tried calling
‪the art director of Sio Atelier,

876
00:55:20,275 --> 00:55:21,693
‪but he didn't pick up.

877
00:55:22,694 --> 00:55:23,695
‪I'll give him a call.

878
00:55:53,892 --> 00:55:55,101
‪REINA CEO CHEON YEO-RI

879
00:55:58,521 --> 00:55:59,647
<i>‪Yes, hello?</i>

880
00:55:59,731 --> 00:56:01,691
‪Si-o, it's me. Cheon Yeo-ri from Reina.

881
00:56:01,775 --> 00:56:03,401
‪Oh, yes. How are you?

882
00:56:03,485 --> 00:56:05,361
‪I called to discuss the hotel's…

883
00:56:18,208 --> 00:56:19,584
‪I mean…

884
00:56:21,461 --> 00:56:24,506
‪I'd like to send a proposal
‪for our next project together.

885
00:56:25,090 --> 00:56:26,716
‪It mentions

886
00:56:26,800 --> 00:56:29,010
‪all the conditions you asked for.

887
00:56:30,637 --> 00:56:32,597
‪Will you think about it positively?

888
00:56:34,057 --> 00:56:34,933
‪If I send it over right now,

889
00:56:36,309 --> 00:56:37,560
‪can you even get it?

890
00:56:38,561 --> 00:56:40,647
‪Yes, I can receive it.

891
00:56:40,730 --> 00:56:43,983
‪But does it include an added incentive?

892
00:56:44,984 --> 00:56:46,903
‪Read through the proposal
‪and give me a call.

893
00:56:47,987 --> 00:56:48,822
‪I'm glad

894
00:56:49,864 --> 00:56:51,157
‪you haven't

895
00:56:51,950 --> 00:56:52,951
‪left yet.

896
00:56:53,701 --> 00:56:55,912
‪Right. I haven't left yet.

897
00:56:57,789 --> 00:57:00,458
‪I clearly warned you last time.

898
00:57:01,042 --> 00:57:04,254
‪I told you I wouldn't let you off
‪if you used me for another con.

899
00:57:04,337 --> 00:57:05,755
‪What will you do then?

900
00:57:06,923 --> 00:57:09,342
‪What are you going to do about it?

901
00:57:09,425 --> 00:57:11,553
‪Who are you calling a con?

902
00:57:12,595 --> 00:57:13,763
‪Si-o!

903
00:57:14,430 --> 00:57:15,473
‪Just this once.

904
00:57:16,391 --> 00:57:18,017
‪I just need one billion won.

905
00:57:18,101 --> 00:57:21,354
‪Then I won't pretend to be you
‪or con anyone again.

906
00:57:23,106 --> 00:57:25,733
‪They'll kill me
‪if I don't pay them back by today.

907
00:57:29,237 --> 00:57:30,613
‪Get help.

908
00:57:31,197 --> 00:57:34,200
‪Get treated and quit gambling,
‪then we'll talk.

909
00:57:43,710 --> 00:57:44,836
‪When?

910
00:57:44,919 --> 00:57:47,338
‪I don't have the time
‪to get treated and quit!

911
00:57:47,422 --> 00:57:49,757
‪They threatened to kill me today!

912
00:57:50,925 --> 00:57:53,636
‪Si-o! Please!

913
00:57:53,720 --> 00:57:55,138
‪Please!

914
00:58:00,435 --> 00:58:01,269
‪Si-o.

915
00:58:02,770 --> 00:58:03,771
‪Sir?

916
00:58:10,278 --> 00:58:11,112
‪Yes?

917
00:58:11,196 --> 00:58:13,031
‪We're all set, sir.

918
00:58:13,114 --> 00:58:14,574
‪Would you like to check right away?

919
00:58:16,242 --> 00:58:17,160
‪Sure.

920
00:58:38,181 --> 00:58:39,933
‪Where's she going in such a hurry?

921
00:58:42,936 --> 00:58:43,853
‪DETAILS OF ACCIDENT

922
00:58:43,937 --> 00:58:45,647
‪CHAIN OF REPORT

923
00:58:48,608 --> 00:58:49,817
‪I was in a yacht accident

924
00:58:50,735 --> 00:58:52,570
‪when I was in university.

925
00:58:52,654 --> 00:58:55,281
‪You resolved a wrongful death
‪from 300 years ago.

926
00:58:55,365 --> 00:58:59,035
‪Don't you think we could solve
‪a 12-year-old case if we really tried?

927
00:59:02,372 --> 00:59:05,542
‪Mr. Ma, it's almost time for the trial.
‪Shouldn't we get going?

928
00:59:05,625 --> 00:59:06,459
‪What?

929
00:59:08,336 --> 00:59:09,629
‪Oh, right. We should.

930
00:59:13,383 --> 00:59:14,300
‪Let's go.

931
00:59:14,384 --> 00:59:15,927
<i>‪The person is unavailable.</i>

932
00:59:16,010 --> 00:59:19,013
<i>‪You will be redirected to voicemail</i>
<i>‪after the beep.</i>

933
00:59:20,765 --> 00:59:22,141
‪Ma, it's me.

934
00:59:22,225 --> 00:59:24,185
‪When you get this message,
‪can you send the police over

935
00:59:24,269 --> 00:59:25,603
‪to the address I sent you?

936
00:59:26,437 --> 00:59:28,273
‪I'm heading to a body disposal site.

937
00:59:29,065 --> 00:59:30,066
‪Call me.

938
01:00:23,953 --> 01:00:24,829
‪Darn it.

939
01:00:33,546 --> 01:00:37,592
‪Why would she come here on her own?
‪It's so dangerous.

940
01:00:38,551 --> 01:00:41,095
‪There has to be more to this.

941
01:01:28,935 --> 01:01:30,937
‪What were you doing at the place

942
01:01:31,020 --> 01:01:32,772
‪that woman's body was found?

943
01:01:32,855 --> 01:01:34,107
‪PRO GOLFER PARK'S EX JANG FOUND DEAD

944
01:01:35,400 --> 01:01:37,527
‪Do you still see ghosts or something?

945
01:01:40,446 --> 01:01:43,116
<i>‪I got you, Cheon Yeo-ri.</i>

946
01:03:30,181 --> 01:03:32,725
‪THANK YOU TO GIL HAE-YEON
‪FOR HER SPECIAL APPEARANCE

947
01:03:33,309 --> 01:03:35,728
‪SPOOKY IN LOVE

948
01:03:35,812 --> 01:03:37,939
<i>‪My Ha-ri filmed this herself.</i>

949
01:03:38,022 --> 01:03:40,107
<i>‪Isn't it so weird and unsettling?</i>

950
01:03:40,191 --> 01:03:42,777
<i>‪Should I actually</i>
<i>‪let off a bomb this time?</i>

951
01:03:43,486 --> 01:03:45,655
‪If we hold an extraordinary
‪shareholders' meeting…

952
01:03:45,738 --> 01:03:47,740
‪It'll be a motion for my removal.

953
01:03:48,449 --> 01:03:51,828
<i>‪Then I'll no longer </i><i>‪be </i><i>‪able</i>
<i>‪to </i><i>‪protect this place.</i>

954
01:03:51,911 --> 01:03:55,331
‪We can't let that happen.
‪I'll fight for Siena too.

955
01:03:55,414 --> 01:03:57,750
‪Let's set a date
‪for the engagement ceremony.

956
01:03:57,834 --> 01:03:59,502
<i>‪Are you free tomorrow?</i>

957
01:03:59,585 --> 01:04:00,419
‪I am.

958
01:04:00,503 --> 01:04:03,297
<i>‪There's something I must do with you.</i>

959
01:04:04,090 --> 01:04:07,218
‪I guess I do need a ring.

960
01:04:08,761 --> 01:04:09,595
<i>‪So this is where…</i>

961
01:04:10,763 --> 01:04:11,597
‪Grandma.

962
01:04:13,891 --> 01:04:16,561
<i>‪I won't let you move in with your in-laws</i>
<i>‪and get stomped all over.</i>

963
01:04:17,979 --> 01:04:18,896
‪I'm not giving up.

964
01:04:18,980 --> 01:04:21,107
‪I'll just have to do things differently
‪from now on.

965
01:04:21,190 --> 01:04:22,525
<i>‪Because my feelings for you…</i>

966
01:04:24,277 --> 01:04:25,486
<i>‪are genuine, Yeo-ri.</i>

967
01:04:26,529 --> 01:04:31,534
‪Subtitle translation by: Jennifer Jean Lim
